      "say": "In 1883 Osborne Reynolds let a thin thread of dye into water flowing through a glass pipe. At low speed the dye stayed a neat line. Speed it up and suddenly the dye burst into swirls. He found one number that predicts which will happen. Look at the two flows side by side.",
